WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.240
Speaker 1: We are now really starting to get
to what is hopefully the end game with the

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.979
coronavirus pandemic.

00:00:06.979 --> 00:00:12.070
As many of you know, a couple of weeks ago,
the CDC as well as Joe Biden in support of

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.070
the CDC.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.430
Remember, Joe Biden doesn't come up with this
stuff on his own.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:22.230
He just goes by what the CDC says, announcing
that outside masking can be dramatically reduced

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.960
for vaccinated people in almost every situation
other than very large crowds gathering mass

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.670
together outdoors.

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:36.160
Over the weekend, Dr. Anthony Fauci now signaled
what is really a major, major step in getting

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.670
to the end of this thing.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:43.890
Dr. Fauci said yesterday that indeed he is
open to starting to reduce indoor masking

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:44.890
rules.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:53.640
We know 999 out of a thousand cases prior
to vaccination were being transmitted indoors

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:58.219
and that we are getting to a level in the
vaccination campaign now with 34 percent of

00:00:58.219 --> 00:01:03.640
the country fully vaccinating at vaccinated,
adding nearly one percent to that every single

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:04.640
day.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:11.970
Dr. Fauci saying that indeed, we do need to
start being more liberal in terms of rules

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:16.510
for wearing masks indoors, but just not quite
yet.

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
Not quite yet.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:23.810
We're down to about 43000 cases a day, the
lowest it's been for a very long time.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:28.829
But at the same time, not quite there yet,
but very soon.

00:01:28.829 --> 00:01:34.820
Dr. Fauci saying it may be time to look at
easing some indoor masking guidelines.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:40.080
And that really will be a sign that we are
very close to the end of this thing, bearing

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.820
in mind, of course, that individuals who remain
at higher risk are going to likely want to

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:49.780
take more precautions, bearing in mind that
in the fall or winter, it may be time for

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:56.570
a booster vaccine tweak, tailored and calibrated
towards the main variants that the primary

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:59.250
variants that have emerged over the last several
months.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:05.979
Friday, the CDC updated its guidance about
how the virus spreads, saying people could

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:13.170
inhale airborne virus even from more than
six feet away from an infected individual.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:17.110
This is something that had been widely reported
by other agencies and researchers.

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:19.720
The CDC now saying it plainly.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:26.170
So in particular, when it comes to endure,
this is where the overwhelming majority of

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.430
the contagion is happening.

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:35.230
That being said, it's Dr. Fauci, as well as
the former head of the FDA, Dr. Scott Gottlieb,

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:42.230
all saying we are very close to statistically
being able to ease off of these indoor masking

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:46.959
requirements, quote, especially if you're
in environments where, you know, you have

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:54.349
a high level of vaccination and that it would
also give public health officials more credibility

00:02:54.349 --> 00:03:01.060
to reinstate more guidelines if there is a
surge in the fall that is problematic and

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:05.390
doesn't isn't well dealt with quickly enough
by the booster shots.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:07.490
And I think that that's an important point.

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:14.260
Both of them saying there's a degree of fatigue
for lack of a better term with a lot of these

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.349
guidelines.

00:03:15.349 --> 00:03:24.409
And when the the data justify easing those,
if we need to put them back in in four months,

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:28.319
six months, eight months or whenever, we hopefully
will have more people listen to us.

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:31.730
Now, I know that that there are parts of the
country where nobody's going to listen and

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.650
nobody's been doing this stuff to begin with.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.970
But for those who have been following CDC
guidelines, like me hearing very concrete

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:41.720
statements like you really don't need to wear
a mask outside now that you're vaccinated,

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.599
David, unless you're together with a crowd
of people, that is great.

00:03:45.599 --> 00:03:46.870
That is a great relief.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:51.730
And that also provides an opportunity to have
a period of time if indeed things are going

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.670
to get worse, where we can feel better about
what's going on.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:59.640
I actually think that from all the evidence
we're seeing, Dr. Eric Topol recently tweeting

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:04.629
very good data about the vaccine's well handling
the British variant, the Brazilian, the South

00:04:04.629 --> 00:04:08.640
African, the New York, the Indian and the
California variants.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:13.099
So if we can keep vaccinating, hopefully all
of this will not come to pass.

00:04:13.099 --> 00:04:17.720
Now, there are people who are not going to
be coming out of this.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:24.130
They're just their remaining home and asked
for the foreseeable future, even as the guidelines

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.180
are going to ease.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:28.020
And I think that that's fine.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:32.490
Some people may do it because of medical conditions,
others because of a sort of pandemic induced

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:34.180
agoraphobia.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:37.290
This is going to be a real issue and it's
going to be an issue for some period of time,

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:43.150
I think the point is no one's going to be
banned from taking any precaution they want

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:44.220
to take.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:49.580
But the numbers I mean, in some states you
are seeing a number of deaths, which is the

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:53.230
same as what you would see during during flu.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:57.330
In other words, there's states where over
the course of a year, five people a day die

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.640
of flu during a normal flu season.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:05.070
And some of those states are now seeing five
to seven coronavirus deaths per day.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:12.730
Once it gets down to that point, it really
becomes more of an individual risk assessment

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:17.540
than statewide or federal guidelines or mandates.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:21.100
And that is going to be the direction things
are shifting.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:27.440
And I think it's perfectly fine for people
to make those risk assessments for themselves.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:31.810
But when you start hearing Dr. Fauci saying
we are soon going to be liberalizing indoor

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:36.100
mass guidelines, when you hear Dr. Scott Gottlieb
say it, you know that you are getting to sort

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.410
of one of the last considerations.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.110
We just have to keep vaccinating

